# Normalize line endings in the repository.
#
# Without this, files committed from Windows are stored with CRLF, and every
# clone on macOS or Linux shows whole files as modified before anyone edits a
# line. Storing LF and letting each checkout use its native endings keeps diffs
# to the lines that actually changed.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Shell scripts must keep LF even on a Windows checkout. CRLF breaks the
# shebang line and the script fails with a confusing "bad interpreter" error.
*.sh text eol=lf
